    "content": "The Holy Thursday Mass, or Mass of the Lord's Supper, celebrated on April 2, 2026, marks the beginning of the Easter Triduum, commemorating the Last Supper, the institution of the Eucharist and Priesthood, and Christ's command to love through service. It features the washing of feet, a procession of the Eucharist, and stripping of the altar. Key Aspects of the Holy Thursday Liturgy: Commemoration: The Mass focuses on Jesus' Last Supper with his disciples, where he instituted the Eucharist and washed their feet. Washing of the Feet (Mandatum): Symbolizing service, the priest washes the feet of 12 people. Transfer of the Eucharist: Following Communion, the Eucharist is carried in procession to a place of adoration (altar of repose). Stripping of the Altar: The main altar is cleared, symbolizing the stripping of Jesus and the beginning of his passion. No Final Blessing: The Mass ends in silence, with adoration continuing through the night, directly linking to Good Friday. Chrism Mass: Earlier in the day, bishops and priests gather at the cathedral to bless the oils for sacraments. Note: While not a holy day of obligation, it is considered one of the most sacred services in the Christian calendar.",
